\newlabel{fig:system}{{1}{2}{The system in one picture. A frozen scenario and a travel-time table feed the event simulator, which acts as referee. $t_0$ is the fixed table of travel times between all 188 places (OSRM $\times $ 1.2); ``hashed'' means its content is fingerprinted so every run uses the same table. ETAs are the plan's predicted curb-arrival times, and ``reads the board'' means the rule sees the open requests and those predictions. The van dispatcher and the Lyft transfer rule (green) are the policies; they see only what a real dispatcher could see. The Lyft service is deliberately thin: the study needs \emph {when} a transferred rider is picked up, not how Lyft matches drivers}{figure.caption.1}{}}
