\newlabel{sec:design}{{7}{10}{}{section.7}{}}
\newlabel{sec:design@cref}{{[section][7][]7}{[1][10][]10}{}{}{}}
\newlabel{tab:rules}{{9}{11}{The six transfer rules. ``Predicted total wait'' is the van plan's predicted pickup clock time minus the request clock time; a request with no feasible van counts as infinitely late, so the rule fires. Codes are used in figures; the number in a code is the threshold in minutes (for R3, the margin by which the van must be later than Lyft). A request is unassigned when no selected van route contains it (it was postponed, \cref {sec:milp}). Expected Lyft pickup = decision time + 2-minute ordering lag + 8-minute median Lyft delay}{table.caption.20}{}}
\newlabel{tab:rules@cref}{{[table][9][]9}{[1][9][]11}{}{}{}}
\newlabel{fig:transfer}{{12}{11}{Timeline of a transferred rider (not to scale). $t_r$ is the request time, $\tau $ the transfer decision, $\ell $ the ordering lag and $\lambda _r$ the rider's hidden Lyft delay; ``booking'' at $\tau +\ell $ is the Lyft order. The request leaves van planning at the decision; the Lyft is ordered one lag later and arrives after the rider's hidden delay. The patience clock keeps running from the original request until a vehicle reaches the curb; a transfer never resets it}{figure.caption.21}{}}
\newlabel{fig:transfer@cref}{{[figure][12][]12}{[1][10][]11}{}{}{}}
